    atlas:level "L2" ;
    atlas:line 889 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.docs@ff0565e/docs/learn/08-babylon-bridge.md> ;
    atlas:status "ran" ;
    atlas:task "Load `src/nurbs.js` in plain Node, build the weighted quarter circle (control points `1 0 0, 1 1 0, 0 1 0`, order 3, knots `0 0 0 1 1 1`, weights `1, 0.7071, 1`) and the same curve unweighted, and report the largest radius error of the weighted one and both midpoints. Then say which of the two midpoints X_ITE's NurbsPositionInterpolator returns." ;
    atlas:title "Check the weights: radius 1.00, not 1.24" ;
    atlas:verify "```js const fs = require('fs'), BR = {}; new Function('BR', fs.readFileSync('src/nurbs.js', 'utf8'))(BR); const q = { pts: [[1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 0], [0, 1, 0]], order: 3, knot: [0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1] }; const w = BR.nurbs.curve({ ...q, weight: [1, Math.SQRT1_2, 1] }), u = BR.nurbs.curve(q); let worst = 0; for (let i = 0; i <= 20; i++) { const p = w.at(i / 20); worst = Math.max(worst, Math.abs(Math.hypot(p[0], p[1]) - 1)); } console.log(worst, w.at(0.5), u.at(0.5)); ``` Run from `x3d.webgpu/bridge` of `x3d.loom@4887a98`." .

