<drill/D-BAB-76> a atlas:Drill ;
    atlas:answer "0.5 0.5 0. The weight the joint does not take stays on the rest position, so the vertex lands halfway along the way from where it was to where the joint would put it." ;
    atlas:checkedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    atlas:checkedText "2026-11-15 python3 -I ((0.5, 0.5, 0.0))" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/08-babylon-bridge.md?plain=1#L988> ;
    atlas:inChapter <chapter/08> ;
    rdfs:label "D-BAB-76 What the skin of one vertex becomes" ;
    atlas:level "L2" ;
    atlas:line 988 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.docs@ff0565e/docs/learn/08-babylon-bridge.md> ;
    atlas:status "ran" ;
    atlas:task "One vertex sits at 1 0 0. One joint with a binding that makes the rest pose the identity is turned 90 degrees about Z, so its matrix J takes 1 0 0 to 0 1 0. The vertex gives that joint a skinCoordWeight of 0.5. Using X_ITE 16.6.0's skin formula, where does the vertex go?" ;
    atlas:title "What the skin of one vertex becomes" ;
    atlas:verify "`python3 -I -c \"v=(1,0,0);w=0.5;Jv=(0,1,0);print(tuple(v[i]+w*(Jv[i]-v[i]) for i in range(3)))\"`" .

