    atlas:level "L2" ;
    atlas:line 338 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.docs@ff0565e/docs/learn/22-typed-judgments-jev.md> ;
    atlas:status "ran" ;
    atlas:task "The behaviour slice counted timers with the chain below. Run it over three tags and say what the old order reports for a `TimeSensor`, then reorder it." ;
    atlas:title "The dead branch" ;
    atlas:verify "the script below. ```python def count(tags, fixed): c = {\"timers\": 0, \"interpolators\": 0, \"sensors\": 0} for t in tags: if t.endswith(\"Interpolator\"): c[\"interpolators\"] += 1 elif fixed and t == \"TimeSensor\": c[\"timers\"] += 1; c[\"sensors\"] += 1 elif t.endswith(\"Sensor\"): c[\"sensors\"] += 1 elif t == \"TimeSensor\": c[\"timers\"] += 1 # unreachable in the old order return c for fixed in (False, True): print(fixed, count([\"TimeSensor\", \"Transform\", \"TouchSensor\"], fixed)) ```" .

