    atlas:level "L2" ;
    atlas:line 356 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.docs@ff0565e/docs/learn/06-xite-the-oracle.md> ;
    atlas:status "ran" ;
    atlas:task "Unpack `x_ite@16.7.0`. Count (a) names registered through `getStaticProperties`, (b) X3DUOM 4.1 concrete nodes, (c) the intersection, (d) the names not in X3DUOM. Then, in a browser, count how many of the 267 names `scene.createNode` accepts after `loadComponents (getProfile (\"Full\"))`." ;
    atlas:title "Count the coverage three ways" ;
    atlas:usesTool <tool/chromium@153>, <tool/swiftshader>, <tool/x3duom@4.1> ;
    atlas:verify "`mkdir t && cd t && npm pack x_ite@16.7.0 && tar xzf x_ite-16.7.0.tgz`, then: ```python import re, glob, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET ST = re.compile(r'getStaticProperties \\(\"(\\w+)\",\\s*\"(\\w+)\",\\s*(\\d+),') files = ['package/dist/x_ite.js'] + [f for f in glob.glob('package/dist/assets/components/*.js') if not f.endswith('.min.js')] names = set() for f in files: names |= {m.group(1) for m in ST.finditer(open(f, encoding='utf-8').read())} uom = ET.parse('X3dUnifiedObjectModel-4.1.xml').getroot() # from x3d_mcp src/validation/schemas concrete = {n.get('name') for n in uom.find('ConcreteNodes')} print(len(names), len(concrete), len(names & concrete), len(names - concrete), sorted(concrete - names)) ```" .

<drill/D-XIT-2> a atlas:Drill ;
    atlas:answer "all three scenes start with frames of 1.0000 (cleared black against a grey Background). Then `visible` settles at 0.1752 (screenshot 0.1752); `blank` and `offcamera` settle at 0.0000 (screenshot 0.0000). A maximum-over-early-frames rule reads 1.0000 for all three, so it calls the blank scenes drawn. Frame counts were 5 to 7 in 2.5 s." ;
    atlas:checkedOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    atlas:checkedText "2026-11-14 `X_ITE 16.4.3`, `16.5.1`, `16.6.1`, `16.7.0`, `16.7.1`, Chromium 153, SwiftShader, 320 x 240" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.docs/blob/ff0565e5a248ca391d68527716a58a821f25d152/docs/learn/06-xite-the-oracle.md?plain=1#L374> ;
    atlas:inChapter <chapter/06> ;
    rdfs:label "D-XIT-2 Catch the sampler that lies" ;
    atlas:level "L2" ;
    atlas:line 374 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.docs@ff0565e/docs/learn/06-xite-the-oracle.md> ;
    atlas:status "ran" ;
    atlas:task "Load three scenes with `Background skyColor=\"0.2 0.2 0.2\"` (a visible 2 m box at `Viewpoint position=\"0 0 6\"`; a `Shape` with no geometry; the box translated 40 m behind the camera). For each, register a `finishEvents` watcher before the load, log the non-background fraction per frame (reference 51/255 grey, tolerance 24/765), and take a screenshot 2.5 s later. Report the maximum, the last frame and the screenshot." ;
    atlas:title "Catch the sampler that lies" ;
    atlas:usesTool <tool/chromium@153>, <tool/swiftshader> ;
    atlas:verify "the watcher (register before `replaceWorld`): ```js const b = X3D.getBrowser (), gl = document.getElementById (\"c\").shadowRoot.querySelector (\"canvas\"); const tmp = document.createElement (\"canvas\"), ctx = tmp.getContext (\"2d\", { willReadFrequently: true }), frames = []; b.finishEvents ().addFieldCallback (\"watch\", () => { try { tmp.width = gl.width; tmp.height = gl.height; ctx.drawImage (gl, 0, 0); const d = ctx.getImageData (0, 0, tmp.width, tmp.height).data; let diff = 0; for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i += 4) if (Math.abs (d[i]-51) + Math.abs (d[i+1]-51) + Math.abs (d[i+2]-51) > 24) diff++; frames.push (+(diff / (d.length / 4)).toFixed (4)); } catch (e) {} }); await b.replaceWorld (await b.createX3DFromString (xml)); ```" .

