    atlas:paidForByText "PhysX 5.12 replayed 1918 steps recorded in Chromium and 969 recorded in Firefox with 0 differing hashes in Chromium, Firefox, WebKit and Node; across machines was not run (C, failure modes 128, 129; [PXB]). The play witness (6 Nov) already compared a final-state hash on one JavaScript engine" ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "A simulation run records a hash of every step's state and is replayed in each host it names, Node included; the first step that differs is reported. A claim in one host is not a claim in another, and a claim on one machine is not a claim on a second" ;
    atlas:violation "a final-state hash; a claim from one place" .

<law/43> a atlas:Law ;
    atlas:caughtBy <diag/PHYS_FALSE_GREEN>, <diag/PHYS_LIMIT_WIDENED>, <diag/PHYS_WAIVERS_OVER_CAP>, <diag/PHYS_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE> ;
    atlas:checkKind "code" ;
    atlas:checkText "code: `PHYS_LIMIT_WIDENED`, `PHYS_FALSE_GREEN`, `PHYS_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE`, `PHYS_WAIVERS_OVER_CAP`; cap 3 passes and cap 0 fails on the real records (re-run, [C])" ;
    atlas:citesSource <source/PXB> ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L133> ;
    atlas:evidenceGrade <grade/C> ;
    atlas:evidenceText "3 of 33 smoke tests failed under load and were accepted as 3 waivers; ragdoll overshoot 0.43 against 0.2 rad (fm 133, 137)" ;
    atlas:forbids "Loosening a threshold to turn red green; a green label on a failing number; a failure with no name on it" ;
    atlas:headline "A tolerance is written before the run; an excursion is a waiver, not a pass" ;
    atlas:inTheme <theme/J> ;
    rdfs:label "Law 43: A tolerance is written before the run; an excursion is a waiver, not a pass" ;
    atlas:line 133 ;
    atlas:n 43 ;
    atlas:paidForBy <fm/133>, <fm/137> ;
    atlas:paidForByText "3 of 33 browser smoke tests failed under load (Galton 220 and 223 of 240 beads against 225; a music box turn 15 of 18 pegs) and the owner accepted them: three waivers under the PhysX profile's cap of three. A ragdoll's limit overshoot reached 0.43 rad against 0.2, and its Gravitron check missed its closed form by 34 % (2.97 against 2.22 rad/s): logged, not tuned (C, failure modes 133, 137; [PXB])" ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "Limits are declared first and may not be widened afterwards. A measure beyond its limit is recorded as an accepted failure with its owner, date, reason and its own numbers; the profile caps how many; a receipt lists them. A self-check that misses its closed form is logged with its probable cause and is never tuned to fit. *Scope: physics profiles only, for now (13 Nov decision); if it proves wrong it is marked a false positive in this table, not deleted*" ;
    atlas:violation "loosening a threshold to turn red green" .

<law/44> a atlas:Law ;
    atlas:caughtBy <diag/PHYS_CONTROL_SURVIVED> ;
    atlas:checkKind "code" ;
    atlas:checkText "code: `PHYS_CONTROL_SURVIVED`; 14 of 14 mutations of the real record caught (re-run, [C]); limits-commit check is not in the kit" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L134> ;
    atlas:evidenceGrade <grade/C> ;
    atlas:evidenceText "the energy check read 1.33e-15 with the buggy rule, 2.0e-15 fixed, 0 with no collisions (fm 148); 125 claims, 25 negative findings survived (src C)" ;
    atlas:forbids "A check that passes for a wrong implementation; a quantity read after the step that enforces it; a limit that cannot be shown to precede the run; a self-graded Confirmed" ;
    atlas:headline "A check is shown able to fail, and a number is not Confirmed until a second reader has tried to break it" ;
    atlas:inTheme <theme/B> ;
    rdfs:label "Law 44: A check is shown able to fail, and a number is not Confirmed until a second reader has tried to break it" ;
    atlas:line 134 ;
    atlas:mentions <fm/157>, <law/43> ;
    atlas:n 44 ;
    atlas:paidForBy <fm/148>, <fm/149>, <fm/150>, <fm/151>, <fm/152>, <fm/153>, <fm/154>, <fm/155>, <fm/156>, <fm/157>, <fm/158>, <fm/159>, <fm/160> ;
    atlas:paidForByText "The Ten Minute Physics ports' own review (13 Nov): 4 reviewers recomputed v1 to v4, 125 claims checked, 25 negative findings survived a second skeptical agent, 0 false alarms. The kinetic-energy check read 1.33e-15 with the buggy collision rule, 2.0e-15 with the fixed one and 0 with no collisions. In batch 6, 2 of 11 mutation controls scaled a limit of 0 and changed nothing (C, failure modes 148 to 160; PHYSICS-PLAYBOOK patterns 11 to 19)" ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "Every reference ships with a wrong implementation it must reject (a control that fails when the code is right is a bug in the control too); a mutation control that changes nothing is counted as missing; a limit file is committed before the run and the runner refuses to start if it differs from its commit; a number the author reads is graded Likely until someone who did not write it has recomputed it. *Scope: physics profiles first, like law 43*" ;
    atlas:violation "a self-graded Confirmed; a mutation control that changes nothing (fm 157: 2 of 11)" .

