<question/1> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L588> ;
    atlas:headline "Promote the five fold-back patches?" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 1: Promote the five fold-back patches?" ;
    atlas:line 588 ;
    atlas:n 1 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "Four pass loom foldback here. Applying them to x3d.onto, the fork or x3d.ML is a PR into your repos, so it waits for your word, and those repos are not checked out on this Mac. Which first? Break-the-Loom's own table suggests Traps and shared acceptance code [BREAK]." .

<question/10> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L597> ;
    atlas:headline "The 33 drafted upstream PRs" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 10: The 33 drafted upstream PRs" ;
    atlas:line 597 ;
    atlas:n 10 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text ": when to \"send\" the first three (304 tests passing together) [MC §9]?" .

<question/11> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L598> ;
    atlas:headline "The Scientific Loom governance patch" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 11: The Scientific Loom governance patch" ;
    atlas:line 598 ;
    atlas:n 11 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "(sha256 5e0aac32…, 4 files, 8 tests) was not delivered. Upload it when found; kit/loomkit/sci.py is a reconstruction until then." .

<question/12> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L599> ;
    atlas:headline "Create hagopjay/x3d.STEM" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 12: Create hagopjay/x3d.STEM" ;
    atlas:line 599 ;
    atlas:n 12 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "(this Mac's account cannot create repos under hagopjay); then the Scientific Loom, sci.py, the profile and X3D-STEM.md can move there by PR." .

<question/13> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L600> ;
    atlas:headline "Send the hardening patch to the Scientific Loom's next pass?" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 13: Send the hardening patch to the Scientific Loom's next pass?" ;
    atlas:line 600 ;
    atlas:n 13 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "It fixes the component declarations and four of the seven assert gates; candidate binding for browser evidence still needs their harness." .

<question/14> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L601> ;
    atlas:headline "Exclude the Loom's evidence directory by path, not by name?" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 14: Exclude the Loom's evidence directory by path, not by name?" ;
    atlas:line 601 ;
    atlas:mentions <fm/74> ;
    atlas:n 14 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "Today any folder called evidence is outside the candidate, so a project's own evidence is unbound unless a witness pins its hashes (failure mode 74). Changing the rule changes the candidate hash of every project that ships an evidence/ folder, including past runs, so it is a versioned decision (loomkit 1.1), not a quiet fix." .

<question/15> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L602> ;
    atlas:headline "~~A waiver status (law 43) is new to the Loom.~~ Decided 13 Nov: physics profiles only, for now. The owner is undecided about the concept, and prefers that, if it proves wrong, it is noted here as a false positive rather than deleted. Today's statuses are pass, fail, deferred, not_applicable, blocked and error; the waiver cap lives in the physics witness's coverage and binds no other profile." ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 15: ~~A waiver status (law 43) is new to the Loom.~~ Decided 13 Nov: physics profiles only, for now. The owner is undecided about the concept, and prefers that, if it proves wrong, it is noted here as a false positive rather than deleted. Today's statuses are pass, fail, deferred, not_applicable, blocked and error; the waiver cap lives in the physics witness's coverage and binds no other profile." ;
    atlas:line 602 ;
    atlas:mentions <law/43> ;
    atlas:n 15 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> .

<question/16> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L603> ;
    atlas:headline "~~The three PhysX waivers are reconstructed~~ Answered 13 Nov: the owner owns all three. They were still reconstructed from the marble thread's note (\"user accepted\") by x3d.physics/tools/physx_run_record.py." ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 16: ~~The three PhysX waivers are reconstructed~~ Answered 13 Nov: the owner owns all three. They were still reconstructed from the marble thread's note (\"user accepted\") by x3d.physics/tools/physx_run_record.py." ;
    atlas:line 603 ;
    atlas:n 16 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> .

<question/17> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L604> ;
    atlas:headline "Cross-machine determinism" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 17: Cross-machine determinism" ;
    atlas:line 604 ;
    atlas:n 17 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "is the one claim every record leaves visible_not_run. Which second machine, and who runs the replay?" .

<question/18> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L605> ;
    atlas:headline "MuJoCo has no run record yet" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 18: MuJoCo has no run record yet" ;
    atlas:line 605 ;
    atlas:n 18 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "Its phase-1 checkpoint replay (mj_getState) is planned; until it lands the physics witness cannot judge a MuJoCo run. Hold the MuJoCo profile until then, or accept a tolerance-style replay row (max_abs_diff against a limit) in loom.physics-run/2?" .

<question/2> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L589> ;
    atlas:headline "The IFC bridge fold-back fails its positive control on this Mac" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 2: The IFC bridge fold-back fails its positive control on this Mac" ;
    atlas:line 589 ;
    atlas:n 2 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "(triangulation differs by platform, §7.4). Fix the witness upstream of promotion (surface comparison), or pin the platform in its profile?" .

<question/3> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L590> ;
    atlas:headline "The family pin" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 3: The family pin" ;
    atlas:line 590 ;
    atlas:n 3 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "Local x3d_mcp is at fa0b389 on fix/physics-findings (17 Oct), not loom-pin-2026-11-01 (decision 5, 1 Nov). Has the tag been created, and should every receipt be re-scored on it [DEF M11]?" .

<question/4> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L591> ;
    atlas:headline "The metadata-containerfield warning" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 4: The metadata-containerfield warning" ;
    atlas:line 591 ;
    atlas:mentions <fm/141> ;
    atlas:n 4 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "fires on Break-the-Loom controls 09 and 12. Should the projects agent confirm it in X_ITE (is a MetadataSet directly under Shape attached), and if so raise it to an error rule? New evidence (13 Nov, failure mode 141): the MuJoCo bridge's x3d_mcp semantic validator reported it as 5 errors per scene while the XSD passed." .

<question/5> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L592> ;
    atlas:headline "Ear thresholds" ;
    rdfs:label "Open question 5: Ear thresholds" ;
    atlas:line 592 ;
    atlas:n 5 ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <doc/x3d.loom@ba30153/LOOM-v1.md> ;
    atlas:text "−14 ±1 LUFS (spec) or −18 to −12 (local study, enforced)? v1 keeps both, tied to their profiles, until you choose a production profile." .

<question/6> a atlas:OpenQuestion ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/hagopjay/x3d.loom/blob/ba301533d7b66eb8fe5e691524a551ef01c58de1/LOOM-v1.md?plain=1#L593> ;
